post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
deepcool-mystique-aio installs three binaries, a per-user daemon unit, a udev
rule and a desktop entry.

  1. Reload udev so the panel is usable:
       sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
       sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=usb --attr-match=idVendor=3633

  2. Start the daemon in your session:
       systemctl --user daemon-reload
       systemctl --user enable --now mystique-daemon

     To start it at boot before anyone logs in:
       sudo loginctl enable-linger $USER

  3. Launch "MYSTIQUE LCD Control" from the menu, or run mystique-ui.

Exactly one process may own the panel. There is no Linux vendor service; if
another driver is running, stop it before starting this daemon.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Stop the daemon before removing the package:
  systemctl --user disable --now mystique-daemon
EOF
}
